mode: "100644"
text: "# Workflows, checklists & worked examples\n\n## The weekly episode loop (repeatable)\nRecord (separate tracks; quiet room; SquadCast/Zoom import) → transcribe → accuracy pass (names/jargon) → Studio\nSound once per source → text edit (tangents out, Underlord filler+silence pass, restructure) → listen-through\nverify → multicam + captions + layout → export long-form → clip set + show notes + chapters from the same\ntranscript → WoopSocial.\n\n## The credit-aware checklist (post-Sept-2025 pricing)\nImport only what you'll edit (media minutes count everything) ✓ · Studio Sound once per source, not per revision\n✓ · batch Underlord actions into fewer, bigger prompts ✓ · Overdub for words/phrases, not paragraphs ✓ · watch\nthe credit meter mid-month ✓ · top-ups expire in 12 months — buy to need ✓ · verify tier limits in-app, not from\nblogs ✓.\n\n## The Overdub decision table\n| Situation | Move |\n|---|---|\n| Flubbed word/product name | Overdub the word (own voice, consented) |\n| Stumbled sentence | Re-record the sentence, or Overdub if short |\n| New intro paragraph | Re-record — long Overdub drifts synthetic |\n| Guest's flub | Ask the guest to re-record/approve; NEVER clone them |\n| Anyone else's voice | Refuse — own-voice-only by design |\n\n## Interview-integrity checklist\nMeaning preserved (would the guest agree that's what they said?) ✓ · clips keep context ✓ · significant edits\noffered for approval ✓ · Underlord's clip flags human-reviewed for fairness ✓ · contractual approval terms\nhonored ✓.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (the flub fix)\n\"said 'InvoiceHero' as 'InvoiceZero' three times. old me re-records 55 minutes. new me: fixed all three in the\ntranscript with overdub — my own trained voice, sounds like me because legally and literally it is me. the new\nintro paragraph though? re-recorded it. typed overdub past one sentence sounds like a polite robot reading my\neulogy.\" — own-voice correction, honest length limit.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (the guest edit)\n\"Our guest gave a lovely, winding answer — eight minutes for two real points. We trimmed it to ninety seconds in\nthe transcript, then did the part that matters: listened back and asked, would she recognize this as what she\nmeant? We sent her the cut anyway — she replied 'oh thank goodness, I ramble.' One small step: before you publish\nanyone else's words, play their edit back with their eyes in mind.\" — concision with meaning preserved, consent\noffered.\n\n## Never\nSkip the transcript accuracy pass · edit by ear what you could edit as text (or ship a text edit you never\nlistened to) · clone anyone else's voice · Overdub full paragraphs · flip a guest's meaning or strip clip context\n· run Studio Sound per revision · import media you won't edit · trust blog tier-numbers over the in-app meter ·\nclaim WoopSocial edits media.\n"
